cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "openBIMtoFEM"
abstract: >-
  Workflow from openBIM (IFC) models of historic masonry buildings to
  OpenSees finite element models, with semantic enrichment of the masonry
  through the Historic Survey, Historic Structure, Historic Masonry and
  Failure Mechanism ontologies, a web editor that records a case study in
  its IFC model, contact interfaces between adjacent structural units, and
  parallel analysis with OpenSeesMP.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Leonardi"
    given-names: "Maria Laura"
    affiliation: "ISISE, Department of Civil Engineering, University of Minho"
version: "1.1.0"
date-released: "2026-10-09"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/mlaura1996/modularBIMtoFEM"
url: "https://openbimtofem.readthedocs.io"
keywords:
  - BIM
  - IFC
  - OpenSees
  - historic masonry
  - ontology
  - finite element method
